        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 东北",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "东北 — dōngběi — \"northeast; the Northeast (of China)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "火车进入了东北 huǒchē jìnrù le dōngběi — The train has come into the northeast of China."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 北 (běi) — five strokes in two halves: on the left a vertical, a short bar into it from the left and a bar rising to the right at its foot; on the right a stroke falling to the left, then a vertical that bends right along the foot and hooks up. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "东北 (dōngběi) is built from 东 'east' and 北 (běi) 'north', both inherited from Middle Chinese, tuwng and pok (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription), which glosses the second 'north' and 'to flee'."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
